1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,640
This is 5x hotter than the Sun.

2
00:00:03,140 --> 00:00:05,679
A lightning bolt heats the air to 50,000 degrees.

3
00:00:06,040 --> 00:00:08,359
The surface of the Sun is about 10,000.

4
00:00:08,662 --> 00:00:11,859
The air heats up so fast, it explodes. That's thunder.

5
00:00:12,419 --> 00:00:14,599
And the bolt is only about an inch wide.

6
00:00:15,060 --> 00:00:18,260
It strikes about 44 times every second, somewhere on Earth.

7
00:00:18,940 --> 00:00:20,280
So next time you see one, remember:
